# She'll Be Coming 'Round the Mountain, strum and sing (repertoire plan: coming-round-the-mountain).
# Your part: G (320003), C (x32010) and D7 (xx0212), down-up eighths all the way, with beats 2
# and 4 a little harder (SixTab cannot put an accent on a strum, so it is written in the words
# above bar 1). Each sung line takes two bars of 4/4, and "She'll be" comes just before each line.
# Line 1 on G; line 2 on G, turning to D7 on its last word, "comes" (the plan says "line 2 on
# D7": the tune of that line sits on G's notes until "when she comes", so D7 waits for "comes");
# line 3 on G, then C for its second half; line 4 G, D7 on "mountain when she", G on "comes".
# Three traditional verses. The tune itself is not written out here: it is traditional and sung
# in many small variants, and this file holds only the accompaniment and the words.
title: She'll Be Coming 'Round the Mountain
id: coming-round-the-mountain
composer: Traditional American
source: Traditional song of the late 19th century, printed in 1927; three traditional verses; accompaniment arranged for Sixstring Academy
arranger: Sixstring Academy
licence: Public domain (traditional); this arrangement is original to Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 3
tags: strumming, eighth notes, i-iv-v, campfire, g, c, d7
tempo: 108
time: 4/4
key: G
pickup: q

